    <!-- Privacy -->
    <string name="privacy_body">• Photos: taken or picked only when you choose. Before analysis, the app strips location metadata, rotates and resizes the image on your device.\n\n• AI analysis: the processed photo or your text is sent over HTTPS to the NutriFit AI proxy, which forwards it to the configured AI provider and returns a structured estimate. The proxy does not store images and redacts content from logs.\n\n• Storage: your diary lives on this device (Room database) and syncs to your private Firebase account. Meal photos are stored in a private folder that only your account can read.\n\n• Assistant: only your goal, remaining targets, diet tags and declared allergies are shared with the assistant — never your name, email or birth date.\n\n• Social: your name and handle are visible to signed-in NutriFit AI users so friends can find you. Posts, photos and clips you share are visible only to you and the friends you had when you posted. In a challenge, your reps, points and a simple pose outline are shared with the other players; your camera video and voice are sent only while you turn them on, directly to the people in the call, and are never recorded.\n\n• Walks: while a walk you started is running, the app uses your location to draw the route and measure distance, pace and speed. The route is saved with the walk in your private account and is never shared unless you share it. Map tiles come from OpenStreetMap data via CARTO.

• Deleting your account removes your cloud data, photos and this device\'s copy.\n\nNutriFit AI provides general nutrition estimates. It does not diagnose conditions and cannot guarantee foods are allergen-free.</string>

